<h2>So is measuring lactate ever worth it?</h2>

<p>Yes. If you're a high-level athlete with high volume and years of base, fighting for the last 2%, lactate gives you resolution a field test can't. It's also how we know field tests work in the first place.</p>

<p>But if you train 6 to 12 hours a week, that 2% isn't your limiter. Your limiter is consistency, sleep, and not spending two months training off zones derived from a test you ran tired and through traffic lights.</p>

<p>Fix that first. The strips will still be there.</p>
